&piece title="A gate: a product with a name" tags="tutorial, diatonic" rung=31 label="Where notes become sound, named: a gate plays its voices with each note of what triggers it." about=&out
&gateNote label="&leadOut is a gate: each note of &tune plays the voices in its braid, &lead and &bell, at three levels of one family: &accent per note, &duck over time, gain=.4 fixed. It is read as [&tune * &accent * &duck * &lead * .4, …]." about=&leadOut
&duckNote label="gate=&duck: how open the gate is, a bar at a time: open, open, ducked to a quarter, open." about=&duck
&productNote label="The bass is the same thing unnamed: a product in the sound card." about=&bass
&bar scan(1 1 1 1) step=free(96bpm, 60..140)
&major scale(major)

&tune over=&major step=&bar/2 0 2 4 2 5 4 2@2 4 5 7 5 4 2 0@2
&accent map=amp step=&bar/2 1 .5 .8 .5
&duck map=amp step=&bar*4 1 1 .25 1
&roots over=&major step=&bar*2 0 3 4 0

&lead s=tri loop=C5 env=&(map=adsr .01 .2 .4 .2)
&bell s=sine loop=C6 env=&(map=adsr 0 .6 0 .3)
&bass s=square loop=C2 lpf=500 env=&(map=adsr .005 .15 .5 .05)

&leadOut trigger=&tune velocity=&accent gate=&duck gain=.4 &lead &bell
&out map=sample level=6 [&leadOut, &roots * &bass * .5]
